Backport of wine 2dc4cfe77d8cc5ca256dca5fbcc1b7134ca3d383
"nsiproxy: Fix check for early IRP cancellation." (Matteo Bruni, 2025-09-05)

IoSetCancelRoutine() returns the *previous* cancel routine.  A non-NULL
return means our routine was still installed, so the cancel routine has
not run and never will, and this thread owns completing the IRP.  The
test was inverted, so an IRP cancelled before the routine was installed
got queued and never completed, while one whose routine had already run
got completed twice.

For the change notification path that leaves a cancelled IRP parked on
notification_queue forever, which wedges the nsi notification thread and
shows up as
  err:sync:RtlpWaitForCriticalSection ... "ntoskrnl.c: irp_completion_cs"
  wait timed out in thread <nsi_notification>, blocked by <sechost_service>

Upstream had already rewritten the icmp echo path by the time of the fix,
so the first hunk lands in nsiproxy_icmp_echo() here rather than in
handle_send_echo(); the check and its justification are identical.

diff --git a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
--- a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
+++ b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
@@ -252,7 +252,7 @@ static NTSTATUS nsiproxy_icmp_echo( IRP *irp )
     EnterCriticalSection( &nsiproxy_cs );

     IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, icmp_echo_cancel );
-    if (irp->Cancel && !IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, NULL ))
+    if (irp->Cancel && IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, NULL ))
     {
         /* IRP was canceled before we set cancel routine */
         InitializeListHead( &irp->Tail.Overlay.ListEntry );
@@ -299,7 +299,7 @@ static NTSTATUS nsiproxy_change_notification( IRP *irp )

     EnterCriticalSection( &nsiproxy_cs );
     IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, change_notification_cancel );
-    if (irp->Cancel && !IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, NULL ))
+    if (irp->Cancel && IoSetCancelRoutine( irp, NULL ))
     {
         /* IRP was canceled before we set cancel routine */
         InitializeListHead( &irp->Tail.Overlay.ListEntry );
